# Rule & Skill Creation Standards

## 3-Tier Rule Architecture

| Tier | Config | Max Lines | Use for |
|------|--------|-----------|---------|
| 1 — Always | `alwaysApply: true`, no globs | 50 | Critical non-negotiable constraints |
| 2 — Auto | `alwaysApply: false` + specific globs | 150 | File-type / path patterns |
| 3 — Agent | `alwaysApply: false`, no globs | 200 | Reference docs loaded on demand |

**Never use `**/*` or `src/**/*` broad globs** — it defeats Tier 2 and bloats every session.

## Canonical vs Cursor

| Location | Role |
|----------|------|
| `.ai/rules/*.md` | **Canonical** — portable across Claude, OpenCode, Copilot |
| `.ai/skills/*/SKILL.md` | **Canonical** — layer workflows, imports, orchestration |
| `.cursor/rules/**/*.mdc` | **Cursor** — tiered `.mdc` with globs + `alwaysApply` |
| `.cursor/skills/*/SKILL.md` | **Cursor** — mirror of `.ai/skills/` for Cursor discovery |

When adding a rule: update `.ai/rules/` first, then add or sync the matching `.cursor/rules/**/*.mdc`.

## Folder Structure (`.cursor/rules/`)

```
global-rules/     ← alwaysApply: true, ≤50 lines (monorepo, code-quality)
api-rules/        ← apps/api/** patterns
dashboard-rules/  ← apps/dashboard/** patterns
database-rules/   ← packages/db-prisma/** patterns
packages-rules/   ← packages/** (non-db) patterns
core-rules/       ← rule/skill authoring (this file)
```

## File Naming

```
{topic}-{always|auto|agent|manual}.mdc
```

Examples: `project-standards-always.mdc`, `nestjs-api-auto.mdc`

## Skills vs Rules

| | Rule (`.mdc` / `.md`) | Skill (`SKILL.md`) |
|--|----------------------|-------------------|
| Purpose | Persistent constraints & patterns | Step-by-step workflow |
| Size | ≤200 lines | ≤500 lines |
| Use for | "Always use api-contracts DTOs" | "How to add a full-stack CRUD entity" |
| Example | dashboard table conventions | `add-crud-feature`, `caveman` |

## Quality Checklist

- [ ] Metadata YAML at top (description, globs, alwaysApply)
- [ ] `alwaysApply: true` only if ≤50 lines and truly global
- [ ] No broad globs (`**/*`, `src/**/*`)
- [ ] Code examples over prose
- [ ] No duplicate content across rules — link to `.ai/` or skills instead
- [ ] ERP golden reference cited: **units** vertical slice
